  "findings": [
    "All twenty responsive images were directly inspected across 320, 390, 1440 and 1920 CSS pixels, including the site font and DejaVu fallback. Text wrapping, control spacing, selected context, study captures and deliberate table scrolling were readable.",
    "All eleven additional lifecycle, missing-clock, fixed-geometry and transfer-state images were directly inspected. The DST gap and irregular-grid reasons are visible; fixed geometry names its separate source instant; transfer preview, accepted context and rejected/expired states preserve readable explanations.",
    "No visual blocker was found in the retained views. The recoverable-error screenshot shows the edited fixed-map configuration, not the offscreen status; error and recovery visibility are established by the browser assertions, not by that image."
  ],
